{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Codebase Cleanup Audit",
  "description": "Monitors the entire codebase for inconsistencies, unnecessary wrappers, superfluous functionality, excessive documentation, and dead code. Triggers comprehensive cleanup analysis when files are modified.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered",
    "patterns": [
      "src/**/*.ts",
      "tests/**/*.ts",
      "*.ts",
      "*.js",
      "*.json",
      "*.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the entire codebase for the following issues and provide specific recommendations with file locations:\n\n1. **Code Inconsistencies**: Look for inconsistent naming conventions, coding patterns, import styles, and architectural approaches across files\n2. **Unnecessary Wrappers**: Identify wrapper functions, classes, or abstractions that add no value and could be simplified or removed\n3. **Superfluous Functionality**: Find unused exports, overly complex implementations that could be simplified, and features that duplicate existing functionality\n4. **Excessive Documentation**: Locate over-documented code where comments are redundant or explain obvious functionality\n5. **Dead Code**: Detect unused imports, unreferenced functions/classes, commented-out code blocks, and orphaned files\n\nFor each issue found, provide:\n- Exact file path and line numbers\n- Description of the problem\n- Specific recommendation for cleanup\n- Impact assessment (low/medium/high priority)\n\nFocus on maintaining the library's core architecture while eliminating bloat and improving maintainability."
  }
}